  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration has obligated $263M in contract dollars in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration executed 50,620 awards with an average award size of $5.2K. Obligations fell 99.1% year over year. The General Services Administration's FY history shows a peak pattern in recent years, with obligations of $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $28.7B in FY26 before the current-year total of $263M. The General Services Administration's FY2027 to date spending concentrates in construction and IT-related services, led by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $57.8M and Computer Systems Design Services at $26M. The General Services Administration's vendor payments in FY2027 to date are concentrated among a handful of firms, led by BLUESTAQ LLC at $24.3M and MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE at $21.4M. This snapshot reflects partial fiscal-year activity and a shift from multibillion-dollar annual totals in prior fiscal years to the current $263M fiscal year to date figure.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the GSA spending level in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration has obligated $263M in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration recorded 50,620 awards with an average award size of $5.2K. Obligations fell 99.1% year over year. The General Services Administration's recent annual obligations were $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $28.7B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which categories and vendors lead GSA's FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads GSA obligations in FY2027 to date at $57.8M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $26M and Other Computer Related Services at $22.6M. The General Services Administration's top vendors in FY2027 to date are BLUESTAQ LLC at $24.3M, MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE at $21.4M, and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $12.1M. Several other vendors and NAICS categories each account for single-digit millions in obligations in the current fiscal year to date."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does General Services Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration has obligated $263M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration executed 50,620 awards with an average award size of $5.2K. Obligations fell 99.1% year over year. Prior full fiscal years show $20.6B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $26.5B in FY24, $23.8B in FY25, and $28.7B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does General Services Administration buy?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration buys a mix of construction, IT services, professional services, and specialty work in FY2027 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $57.8M, Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $26M, Other Computer Related Services accounts for $22.6M, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $19.7M. The General Services Administration also shows R&D, wholesale trade brokers, consulting, engineering, custom programming, and automobile manufacturing among the top categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are General Services Administration's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration's largest contractors in FY2027 to date are BLUESTAQ LLC, MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE, and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION. BLUESTAQ LLC received $24.3M, MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE received $21.4M, and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION received $12.1M. Other top vendors include INSURANCE AUTO AUCTIONS, INC. at $10.5M, VIVSOFT TECHNOLOGIES LLC at $10.5M, ECS FEDERAL, LLC at $10M, W.W. GRAINGER, INC. at $8.9M, ERNST & YOUNG LLP at $8.8M, CCI FACILITY CONTRACTORS, LLC at $8.7M, and MANTECH ADVANCED SYSTEMS INTERNATIONAL, INC. at $7.2M."
